SUMMARY:Flags on the 48 - A September 11 Memorial Hike: South Kinsman
LOCATION:Lafayette Place Campgroun\nFranconia\, NH 03580
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 12\, 2026\nhttps://activities.outdoors.or
 g/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001FKlp2AG/\nWe are organizing a team for the Flag
 s on the 48 memorial event. Join our Chapter in honoring those who died on
  Sept 11 by helping to raise our flag over South Kinsman. Out and back hi
 ke via the Lonesome Lake\, Fishin' Jimmy and Mt. Kinsman trails\, 10 mi.\,
  ~ 3\,200' elevation gain\, with average\, strenuous\, and very strenuous
  terrain\, at a slower-moderate pace (1-2 mph). Limited to 12\, including 
 the leaders\, physically fit hikers with current\, i.e.\, within the past 
 year\, upcountry hiking experience. All participants will be screened for 
 this hike to ensure we can stay together as a group\; otherwise\, it can c
 reate an unsafe situation.This is a full day event with an early start. Le
 ave room in your pack to carry group gear: flag\, PVC pipe used to constru
 ct the flagpole\, guy lines and other hardware for securing the pole. We w
 ill arrive at the peak to allow time to set up/secure the flagpole at the 
 summit and raise the flag before 12 noon. The flag then flies from noon th
 rough 2 pm. We then will lower the flag\, deconstruct the flag pole\,guy l
 ines\, etc. and pack up our gear.Required gear:• Bring what you need to 
 stay warm\, dry\, and happy for an extended day on the summit• A pack la
 rge enough to hold all your gear + group gear• 3-4 liters of water• Sn
 acks and trail lunch• Pad to sit on• Sunscreen• Bug repellent• Hea
 dlamp• Rain gear• Layers to add & subtract to regulate your body tempe
 rature throughout the day\, including\, and not limited to\, a puffy jacke
 t\, winter hat/mittens/gloves
END:VEVENT
